(5445857, 782391, 83544, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, the idea is great but the shirt is what bothers me and it''s really distracting. He could have taken a better clothes or you to crop just the face (sorry about my previous unfinished comment)</td>', 'Hmmm, the idea is great but the shirt is what bothers me and it''s really distracting. He could have taken a better clothes or you to crop just the face (sorry about my previous unfinished comment)', '2009-04-20 19:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5445865, 781411, 101256, '<td valign="top">As a friend of abstracts, this is simple an outstanding example of indirect lighting creating a truly abstract image which is both intriguin and somewhat thought provoking. A great example of how lighting can be used to great effect in a creative way. The only complaint is the left side of the image which could be viewed as a flaw, but adds some dimension and attempts to fill a void in space. Well thought out and executed, if there were any justice, it would be a ribbon winner. Well done.</td>', 'As a friend of abstracts, this is simple an outstanding example of indirect lighting creating a truly abstract image which is both intriguin and somewhat thought provoking. A great example of how lighting can be used to great effect in a creative way. The only complaint is the left side of the image which could be viewed as a flaw, but adds some dimension and attempts to fill a void in space. Well thought out and executed, if there were any justice, it would be a ribbon winner. Well done.', '2009-04-20 19:12:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5445866, 781612, 101256, '<td valign="top">More a image of lighting than a creative use of lighting. It''s hard to rate this because of it''s nature. It might have been a better approach to find a subject and then use the lighting to create the image rather than of the light itself.</td>', 'More a image of lighting than a creative use of lighting. It''s hard to rate this because of it''s nature. It might have been a better approach to find a subject and then use the lighting to create the image rather than of the light itself.', '2009-04-20 19:12:15.000000', NULL, 1),
