(5451258, 781600, 22301, '<td valign="top">You have to use Save For Web, not just the regular save to get your image ready for challenges. For example, all of your exif data is still attached to your image.(It was taken at 9:46 PM and was a 20 sec exposure) This data is wasting file space that could be used for image quality. Check out this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> for getting challenge entries ready for challenges. It is for an older version of photoshop, but it works the same for your version of CS2. It will allow you to get those files right up to size limits. Good Luck.</td>', 'You have to use Save For Web, not just the regular save to get your image ready for challenges. For example, all of your exif data is still attached to your image.(It was taken at 9:46 PM and was a 20 sec exposure) This data is wasting file space that could be used for image quality. Check out this tutorial for getting challenge entries ready for challenges. It is for an older version of photoshop, but it works the same for your version of CS2. It will allow you to get those files right up to size limits. Good Luck.', '2009-04-24 18:10:38.000000', NULL, 0),
